(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [11 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [12 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [13 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [15 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [21 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [22 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [23 1 "// or Repl."] [45 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [48 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [49 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [63 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [82 1 "// unsupportedOperation is io.UnsupportedOperation's stand-in until _pyio (PY6): a ValueError (its base, with OSError)."] [85 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [158 1 "// The standard streams' buffer (PY6e's REQUEST: subprocess's children write sys.stdout.buffer): a binary"] [159 1 "// view of the same bufio reader or writer, so text and bytes keep their order."] [257 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [278 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [331 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): a namespace standing in for the struct sequence"] [343 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, as namespaces of CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [374 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): the tools' registry and the events' numbers; no event is ever raised (pyi has no"] [375 2 "// instrumentation yet: the debugging family's)"] [448 2 "// pyi's own launcher when bin/pyi runs it (PY6e: tools/pyi/python3, CPython's command line), so that"] [449 2 "// script_helper and subprocess start pyi as CPython starts itself"] [511 5 "// traceback objects are PY5b's (a Traceback is not an Object yet)"] [521 26 "// -X cpu_count unset (os.process_cpu_count from sched_getaffinity)"] [524 3 "// gh-135228 (dataclasses' slots): the class's __dict__ and __weakref__ descriptors removed"] [579 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [627 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [628 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [645 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [653 1 "// writeTo writes s to a file object: the interpreter's stdout when f is nil or None, a textFile directly,"] [654 1 "// else f.write(s)."] [675 1 "// exactArgsN checks a function's call: n positional arguments, no keywords (CPython's messages)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[102 53] [120 30] [183 54] [201 34] [250 30] [280 48] [346 13] [346 26] [432 20] [473 62] [479 62] [493 26] [500 54] [503 26] [509 26] [510 38] [525 68] [533 41] [540 51] [543 29] [549 56] [555 43] [558 46] [570 7] [570 30] [584 35] [638 63] [647 48] [663 28]]} (go/file "sys.go" :imports [


